    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦ</span></b> , τό, name of the
		letter <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			2.4321.24
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>, Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
			Ath.
			10.454f
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hellad.
		</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
			Phot.
			<u>Bibl.</u>
			p.530
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			B.
		</span></i>, etc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὺ
			μῦ</span>, to represent <i>a muttering sound</i> made with the
			lips, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦ λαλεῖν</span>
			<i>to mutter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
				80
			</span></i> (dub. l.); to imitate the sound of <i>sobbing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὺ μῦ, μὺ μῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			.</div>
